From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:13:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/29] Lab: with XCL_VIEW_FULL_RANGE=1 a tile without a source
 is not checked again while fresh

A run with 64 MiB behind each root address (XCL_VIEW_ROOT_KB=65536) checked
103 M tiles without a source (about 4.6 M with 1 MiB) and its pace fell
apart: such a tile was looked up again at every range that named it, as
nothing remembered a miss. With the switch a miss is kept (Misses, at most
200 000 tiles, then cleared) and the tile not looked up again for
XCL_VIEW_FRESH_MS, as a tile with a source is not checked again; a kept miss
past the old bound ends a full range as a lookup would. Without the switch
nothing changes.

The stats line adds, atomics only: lookups without a source past the old
bounds (where full ranges end, apart from "without a source"), misses not
looked up again, the longest range in MB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
